# --- Per-install secrets and machine-specific artifacts ---
# Note: git has no trailing-comment syntax, so a comment on a pattern line
# becomes part of the pattern and silently matches nothing. Comments go above.
kam_token.txt

# The native-host manifest and its launcher, both written by register_host.py.
# They embed absolute paths to this machine and this Python install, so they
# must never be committed. Both manifest spellings are listed because
# register_host.py writes the dotted form.
com.kam.tts.json
com_kam_tts.json
kam_host.bat

# Measured per machine by hardware_profile.py, or auto-detected on first boot.
hardware_profile.json

# The private half of the extension signing key. Only the public half belongs in
# the repo, and it already sits in manifest.json as the "key" field, which is
# what pins the extension id. The private key signs .crx builds and is kept
# outside the repo entirely, so these patterns are a backstop against it ever
# being copied in here by mistake.
*.pem
*.key
kam_extension_key*

# --- Runtime state and learned data ---
tts_quality.db
tts_quality.db-*
good_settings.json
user_defaults.json
voice_baseline*.json
kam_server.log
.kam_ready
.kam_stage
.kam_lock
.warmup_done

# --- Personal audio and voice clones ---
# Audio stays out by default. The one deliberate exception is below.
*.wav
voice_samples_*/
voices/
voice_latents*.pt
my_voice.wav

# The default voice ships with the project on purpose, so a fresh clone can be
# heard speaking without recording anything first. See VOICE.md for what may and
# may not be done with these recordings; the code is MIT, the voice is not.
#
# Two gotchas are baked into these three lines, so please don't "tidy" them.
#
# First, the paths start at server/ rather than reading voice_samples/. A
# pattern with a slash anywhere but the end is anchored to the directory holding
# the .gitignore, so !voice_samples/*.wav only ever matches a folder at the repo
# root and leaves the real clips under server/ still caught by *.wav above.
#
# Second, the folder has to be re-included before the files, since git will not
# re-include anything underneath a directory that is itself excluded.
!server/voice_samples/
!server/voice_samples/*.wav
!server/voice_samples/*.txt

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
